{"title":"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems\">2002 AMC 12A #3</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">2002 AMC 10A #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Recursive_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Recursive Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>According to the standard convention for exponentiation, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29dee8eac6c7812722f0013ad002044b30d8f220.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{2^{2^{2}}} = 2^{(2^{(2^2)})} = 2^{16} = 65536.\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>If the order in which the exponentiations are performed is changed, how many other values are possible?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b43c42263ca15ff716ac204e8358d6d66b86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 1\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 2\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 3\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The best way to solve this problem is by simple brute force. \n</p><p>It is convenient to drop the usual way how exponentiation is denoted, and to write the formula as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95ad6ef62ef46568f4225fb48c5035c466cd6594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\uparrow 2\\uparrow 2\\uparrow 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39cad522ccbe5a31209793365754665a4d65556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\uparrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"9\" height=\"17\" /> denotes exponentiation. We are now examining all ways to add parentheses to this expression. There are 5 ways to do so:\n</p>\n<ol><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b051cc37e3e1d846f5ad278cd99b38452212ea85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\uparrow (2\\uparrow (2\\uparrow 2))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02627e764c70ea23d57e018ebe3c404e9711ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\uparrow ((2\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/0347537c5d3c7210d985a80c52a7ce8b0c5ad508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((2\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3aa5d6c5c79cf4887a0cb32d96cdcc64ae2527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\uparrow (2\\uparrow 2))\\uparrow 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79edd4a1120216c42cac680d09944f37a7754ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow (2\\uparrow 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /></li></ol>\n<p>We can note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378c9aecdd9367ed7bd377c63445c4fcd005d3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\uparrow (2\\uparrow 2) = (2\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow 2 =16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore options 1 and 2 are equal, and options 3 and 4 are equal.\nOption 1 is the one given in the problem statement. Thus we only need to evaluate options 3 and 5.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2df7432bf23dd99404db9a849a46559491c910a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((2\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow 2 = 16\\uparrow 2 = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1daea895707743f04d22f20424cd895e320c7b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\uparrow 2)\\uparrow (2\\uparrow 2) = 4 \\uparrow 4 = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus the only other result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd678361b0f40ec2723283c0f2bab3df5cadc68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619254fd3d431079b23def51e7eedb31d1088158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Recursive_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Recursive_Method)\">Solution 2 (Recursive Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Recursive Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will proceed by recursion using the same notation as Solution 1. Note that we can either have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec14d4bf0b5fd42110fc8e4ce43692ddd2667b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 \\uparrow 2 \\uparrow 2) \\uparrow 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c6d81ae1b3e250e8ea50c2a56646852ed401272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\uparrow (2 \\uparrow 2 \\uparrow 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>However, the expression in the parentheses can either be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1ca2ecae394a0090aeb4f57c7b55b397a1e0877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 \\uparrow 2) \\uparrow 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397462780c3a01a801e928abab501482b9dddd27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\uparrow (2 \\uparrow 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />, which correspond to the same value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we can either have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bade9c1fe9e69f976dbef4cf4458c5671671ecf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfc79bbd3ccc9d92286e70e51d81a3a9648d5d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{16}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e101201addd96f637069ef5899fa2b44223efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~TPColor\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fJndjYHWBrU\">https://youtu.be/fJndjYHWBrU</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A\">2002 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Proble